# The clipboard (device-layer-0005): text in and out of the platform's own pasteboard, the one a person copies and
# pastes with in every other app. The same two calls on every target; each platform answers with its own:
#
#   macOS     NSPasteboard.general        iOS       UIPasteboard.general
#   Android   ClipboardManager            desktop   the AWT system clipboard (Compose on Linux, Windows, macOS)
#   browser   navigator.clipboard (a secure page, and the browser's own permission)
#
# A host with no clipboard (the server, a worker, the memory host) answers `unavailable` and reads empty text.
#
#   read-clipboard           the text on the clipboard now, or empty text when it holds none
#   write-clipboard(text)    `written`, `denied` (the platform refused, a browser page out of focus or without the
#                            grant) or `unavailable`

load ./native/{platform}/clipboard
  find read-clipboard-text
  find write-clipboard-text

task read-clipboard
  like text
  send back
    call read-clipboard-text

task write-clipboard
  take text, like text
  like text
  send back
    call write-clipboard-text
      read text
